# the Chords page (EDIT tapped): eight slots. Endless (the default): the walk's eight, slot 1 playing; on a change all
# move up a slot (a gap stays a gap) and the walk writes slot 8. KNOB 1 the slot, the keys its root (a walk's chord
# keeps its kind and type), KNOB 2 its kind (Empty: a gap), KNOB 3 its type, KNOB 4 Play: Endless or Loop (the slots
# in turn, nothing new); ALGORITHM the walk's character (Home, Wander, Free), its chords walked again at once (yours
# and the gaps kept). EDIT again: back; EDIT held: the next chord; kept by the piece
listen
wait 3000
tap EDIT
wait 400
expect view 15
tap EDIT
wait 200
expect view 15
# slot 1: the walk's home chord, Dm7 in D Aeolian (Timewind), as it would be written
said Chords page, walk Home: Slot 1, Chord Minor, Type 7, Play Endless
expect par64 1
expect par72 0
expect progpos 0
# a key on it: written, its root F (the keys here are the notes, not the scale), its kind and type kept
tapkey w0
wait 200
said Fm7
expect par64 5
expect par72 2
expect par80 2
spin K3 2
wait 200
said Type 9
expect par80 4
# slot 2: the walk's; a key writes it (root Bb), Empty makes it a gap
turn K1 1
wait 200
said Slot 2
tapkey b2
wait 200
expect par65 10
expect par73 >0
spin K2 -100
wait 200
said Chord Empty
expect par73 0
expect par65 0
# Play: Loop and back (the walk's character kept)
spin K4 1
wait 200
said Play Loop
expect par88 4
spin K4 -1
wait 200
said Play Endless
expect par88 0
# ALGORITHM: the walk Wander, its chords walked again; slot 1 (yours, Fm9) and slot 2 (a gap) kept; back to Home
turn ALGO 1
wait 200
said WALK Wander: roams wider
expect par88 1
expect par64 5
expect par72 2
expect par80 4
expect par65 0
expect par73 0
turn ALGO -1
wait 200
said WALK Home: stays near home
expect par88 0
tap HOME
wait 300
expect view 0
# the next chord (EDIT held): all up a slot; slot 1 is the gap now (the Fm9 holds), the walk wrote slot 8
press EDIT
wait 700
release EDIT
wait 200
said NEXT CHORD
wait 4500
expect progpos 0
expect par64 0
expect par72 0
expect chordroot 5
expect par71 >0
expect par79 0
# EDIT held on (1.5 s): new chords, the walk's walked again (not the one playing), and no next chord on release
press EDIT
wait 1800
release EDIT
wait 200
said NEW CHORDS Home
said_none NEXT CHORD
expect progpos 0
expect par64 0
expect par72 0
tap PLAY
wait 6000
expect store_writes >0
reboot
wait 1000
expect par64 0
expect par72 0
expect par71 >0
expect par88 0
# REC held on the Chords page and the Pattern page: the effects grid alone, drawn once (they used to draw over each
# other, flickering)
tap EDIT
wait 300
expect view 15
press REC
wait 400
expect blits !=-1
wait 1000
expect blits <3
release REC
wait 300
expect view 15
tap HOME
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
tap SEQ
wait 300
expect view 16
press REC
wait 400
expect blits !=-1
wait 1000
expect blits <3
release REC
wait 300
tap SEQ
